  "description": "MATJEZ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C64 H86 Dy4 N10 O20,4(C1 H4 O1),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.726-3.916 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 103.20-110.64°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy4(LH)2(μ3-OH)2(Piv)4(MeOH)2]·4MeOH·2H2O (C68H106Dy4N10O26). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 Piv (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 Piv (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
